{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"93d02f3a-9675-44d6-b82f-6e7e1361add4","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Every triangle has three interior angles. Let's call them alpha, beta, and gamma, and see why their sum is always 180 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Angles in a triangle"},{"op":"diagram","id":"triangle","region":"right","primitives":[{"kind":"line","points":[[0.2,0.8],[0.45,0.3],[0.8,0.8],[0.2,0.8]],"stroke":"solid","meaning":"triangle with a horizontal base"},{"kind":"arc","center":[0.2,0.8],"radius":[0.1,0.1],"start_deg":-63.4,"end_deg":0,"stroke":"solid","label":"α"},{"kind":"arc","center":[0.8,0.8],"radius":[0.1,0.1],"start_deg":-180,"end_deg":-125,"stroke":"solid","label":"β"},{"kind":"arc","center":[0.45,0.3],"radius":[0.12,0.12],"start_deg":55,"end_deg":116.6,"stroke":"solid","label":"γ"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"93d02f3a-9675-44d6-b82f-6e7e1361add4","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Draw a line through the top vertex parallel to the base. Alternate interior angles place alpha and beta beside gamma.","ops":[{"op":"line","id":"parallel","canvas_id":"triangle","from":[0.08,0.3],"to":[0.92,0.3],"stroke":"dashed","label":"parallel to base"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"alpha_copy","canvas_id":"triangle","center":[0.45,0.3],"radius":0.15,"start_deg":116.6,"end_deg":180,"stroke":"solid","label":"α"},{"op":"angle_arc","id":"beta_copy","canvas_id":"triangle","center":[0.45,0.3],"radius":0.15,"start_deg":0,"end_deg":55,"stroke":"solid","label":"β"},{"op":"text","id":"reason","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Alternate interior angles are equal"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What kind of angle do the three adjacent angles beneath the parallel line form?","expected_gist":"A straight angle, measuring 180 degrees."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"93d02f3a-9675-44d6-b82f-6e7e1361add4","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Together, these three angles fill a straight angle. A straight angle measures 180 degrees, so the triangle's interior angles sum to 180 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"angle_arc","id":"straight","canvas_id":"triangle","center":[0.45,0.3],"radius":0.26,"start_deg":0,"end_deg":180,"stroke":"dashed","label":"180°"},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"reason","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=180^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":null}}
